3. DATABASE KO SCALE KAISE KAREIN ?
====================================

Database ki capacity increase karne ki Broadly do approaches hoti hain:

---------------------
#1. VERTICAL SCALING
---------------------

Vertical scaling ka meaning hai existing database server ko more powerful banana.

Example:

Initially:
    CPU  : 8 cores
    RAM  : 32 GB
    Disk : 500 GB

After scaling:
    CPU  : 32 cores
    RAM  : 128 GB
    Disk : 2 TB



## VERTICAL SCALING KA BENIFIT
---------------------------------

Vertical scaling relatively simple hota hai because
application architecture mein major changes nahi karne padte.

Architecture same rehti hai:

Application
     |
     v
Single DB
     |
     v
More Powerful DB



## VERTICAL SCALING KI LIMITATIONS
------------------------------------

1. COST
---------

More powerful hardware generally more expensive hota hai.

2. SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE
----------------------------

Resources increase karne ke baad bhi database ek single node ho sakta hai.

Agar wahi DB unavailable ho gaya, to application ka database access fail ho sakta hai.

Therefore:

Vertical Scaling
    → Capacity increase karta hai
    → But by itself High Availability solve nahi karta.



------------------------
#2. HORIZONTAL SCALING
------------------------

Ek database server ko bigger banane ke bajaye
multiple database nodes/servers use karke
database ki capacity ya availability ko improve karna.

Conceptually:

             Application
                  |
          +-------+-------+
          |       |       |
          v       v       v
        DB-1    DB-2    DB-3


Horizontal scaling ke different approaches ho sakte hain:

1: Replication → Read Replicas
2: Sharding / Partitioning



