         +-----------+-----------+
         |                       |
       READ                    WRITE
         |                       |
         +-----------+-----------+
                     |
                     v
                 Single DB

Ab application popular ho gayi aur traffic significantly increase ho gaya.

Assume karo:

    100,000 requests/sec

        90,000 → READ
        10,000 → WRITE


Ab 90,000 read requests bhi isi single database ko hit karengi,
to database ke CPU aur memory par significant load aa sakta hai,
aur application ka configured DB connection pool bhi saturate ho sakta hai.

Isse database bottleneck ban sakta hai:

    Higher DB Load
         ↓
    Higher Query Latency
         ↓
    Lower Application Throughput


